<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear all Commands, show "No Mode" and disable sequence ("hands off" outputs)]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Labels/>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)CLR(Wrk_SMProgCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SMOperCmd) OTU(OCmd_SeqPause) OTU(OCmd_SeqResume) OTU(OCmd_SeqAutoPause) OTU(OCmd_SeqCancelPause) ,CLR(MCmd_InpForce) OTU(MCmd_TimerForce) OTU(MCmd_SeqStepForce) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands, we're not READY for them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_SeqStart) OTU(Rdy_SeqHold) OTU(Rdy_SeqRestart) OTU(Rdy_SeqStop) OTU(Rdy_SeqReset) ,OTU(Rdy_SeqPause) OTU(Rdy_SeqResume) OTU(Rdy_SeqAutoPause) OTU(Rdy_SeqCancelPause) OTU(Rdy_SeqStepForce) ,CLR(Rdy_Output) CLR(Rdy_RealOutput) ,OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the sequence and step timers.

##### V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[RES(Wrk_StepT)RES(Wrk_SeqFaultT);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the sequence state as Idle, Not Ready, Not Available for Program Control.

##### V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTU(Nrdy_Perm) OTU(Nrdy_Intlk) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) ,OTL(Sts_SeqIdle) OTU(Sts_SeqStarting) OTU(Sts_SeqRunning) OTU(Sts_SeqComplete) ,OTU(Sts_SeqStopped) OTU(Sts_SeqHeld) OTU(Sts_SeqExecuting) OTU(Sts_SeqPaused) ,CLR(Val_State) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.

##### V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_IntlkTrip) OTU(Alm_SeqTO) OTU(Alm_StepTO) ,OTU(Sts_IntlkTrip) OTU(Sts_SeqTO) OTU(Sts_StepTO) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Manage sequence state and execute sequence; handle sequence editing from HMI]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Labels>
<Label Name="AfterClear"/>
<Label Name="AfterEditFix"/>
<Label Name="AfterInitArray"/>
<Label Name="AfterReal"/>
<Label Name="ClearLoop"/>
<Label Name="DoIA"/>
<Label Name="DoOutputs"/>
<Label Name="EditLoop"/>
<Label Name="NoEdit"/>
<Label Name="NoGo"/>
<Label Name="RealOuts"/>
<Label Name="SkipFFRew"/>
</Labels>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_Seq:  PROCESS -- SIMPLE SEQUENCER
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-31:  External Access set to Read/Write for discrete
and REAL outputs. Several Parameter Descriptions changed.
V3.0-02  2013-10-30:  Modified restart initialization for case where
sequence is started on a step other than Step 1.
Modified discrete output handling for masking.
Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms.
V3.0-03  2014-01-30:  Modified to work with new P_Prompt for
manual (prompted) input.
V3.0-04  2014-02-28:  Modified handling of branch targets when
inserting or deleting steps online.
V3.0-05  2014-04-04:  Added resetting of entered Quantity to "standard"
on Operator command or on change to standard quantity
(available when sequence is Idle). Fixed Rdy_NextStep.
V3.0-06 2014-06-12:  Modified limit checking on Standard Quantity.
V3.1-00  2014-07-16:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1,
added Not Ready (Nrdy_) bits, added Err_NextStep.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Using P_Alarm, P_Mode 3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
See Reference Manual for details on this instruction.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(s:fs) ,XIO(Wrk_Init) ,XIC(Err_StepSizeFault) ][CLR(Wrk_StepNum) MOV(1,Wrk_RestartStep) MOV(1,Wrk_IntlkStep) MOV(1,MSet_NextStep) CLR(Val_StepTRemain) ,CLR(Val_InStepT2TO) CLR(Wrk_PauseBits) SIZE(Ref_Steps,0,Wrk_scr1) SUB(Wrk_scr1,1,Wrk_MaxStepIndex) MOV(Wrk_MaxStepIndex,Wrk_LastStep) ,CLR(Wrk_HMI_scr1) COP(Wrk_NullName,Val_CurrStepName,1) CLR(Wrk_QualifiedInputs) COP(Wrk_NullStep,Cur_Step,1) OTU(Cur_HasTimer) ,MOV(Cfg_StdQty,OSet_Qty) MOV(Cfg_StdQty,PSet_Qty) MOV(Cfg_StdQty,Wrk_StdQtyOld) MOV(1.0,Wrk_ScaleFactor) MOV(100,Val_QtyPct) ,SIZE(Ref_Steps[0].Cfg_RealOut,0,Inf_MaxCntRealOut) XPY(2,Inf_MaxCntRealOut,Wrk_scr1) SUB(Wrk_scr1,1,HMI_RealOutVis) AND(Cfg_ScaleRealOut,HMI_RealOutVis,Cfg_ScaleRealOut) CLR(Wrk_SMStateNum) MOV(1,Wrk_SMState) MOV(1,Cur_EditStep) ,MOV(11,HMI_InStepNum) LES(Wrk_MaxStepIndex,11) MOV(Wrk_MaxStepIndex,HMI_InStepNum) ,XPY(2,HMI_InStepNum,Wrk_scr1) SUB(Wrk_scr1,1,HMI_InStepVis) GRT(Wrk_MaxStepIndex,11) OTL(HMI_InStepVis.31) ,MOV(1,Wrk_scr1) OTL(Wrk_InitArray) ,OTL(Wrk_Init) OTU(Sts_Bypass) CLR(Wrk_SeqLoopCnt) MOV(1,Inp_SeqLoopCnt) ,LES(Wrk_MaxStepIndex,1) OTE(Err_StepSizeFault) JMP(NoGo) ];]]>
</Text>
