<Programs Use="Context">
<Program Use="Context" Name="InstructionSamples">
<Routines Use="Context">
<Routine Use="Context" Name="P_Seq">
<RLLContent Use="Context">
<Rung Use="Target" Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_Seq:  PROCESS -- SIMPLE SEQUENCER
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.0.
V3.0-01  2013-07-31:  External Access set to Read/Write for discrete
and REAL outputs. Several Parameter Descriptions changed.
V3.0-02  2013-10-30:  Modified restart initialization for case where
sequence is started on a step other than Step 1.
Modified discrete output handling for masking.
Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms.
V3.0-03  2014-01-30:  Modified to work with new P_Prompt for
manual (prompted) input.
V3.0-04  2014-02-28:  Modified handling of branch targets when
inserting or deleting steps online.
V3.0-05  2014-04-04:  Added resetting of entered Quantity to "standard"
on Operator command or on change to standard quantity
(available when sequence is Idle). Fixed Rdy_NextStep.
V3.0-06 2014-06-12:  Modified limit checking on Standard Quantity.
V3.1-00  2014-07-16:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1,
added Not Ready (Nrdy_) bits, added Err_NextStep.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Using P_Alarm, P_Mode 3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
See Reference Manual for details on this instruction.
============================================================
This instruction executes a user-defined sequence using
32 BOOL outputs to drive equipment / operations, 32 REAL
output to issue setpoints / parameters, and 32 BOOL inputs
for feedback checking in order to satisfy conditions to go
from step to step.

The steps of the sequence are stored in a separate array.
This allows any number of steps to be allocated for a given
sequence, allowing optimum use of memory.  The array must
have at least TWO elements.  (Element 0 is used internally,
and Step 1 must exist.)

     IMPORTANT:     Use of a sequence array with more
than 500 elements will result in large scan time bumps when
editing from the HMI and is STRONGLY discouraged!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Seq(MyP_Seq,MyP_Seq_Steps);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
